\p{\strong{Status:} open.}
\p{On 2026-11-23 the repository had no workflow, and the pull requests had no status checks. That a branch builds, and that it uses no \code{\verb~|sorry~}, rests on what its description says and on whoever builds it locally. A workflow should run \code{\verb~|lake build~} with the Mathlib cache, which also runs the \code{\verb~|…Examples.lean~} files and the checks of axioms, and \code{\verb~|journal-build~} for this forest. Whether it uses the flake or a toolchain installed by elan is open; the flake is what the proofs are developed with.}
